===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|anglen|t=to meet at an angle, converge}}, from the noun (see above).

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|often in the [[passive]]}} To place (something) at an angle.
#: {{ux|en|The roof is '''angled''' at 15 degrees.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To change direction rapidly.
#: {{ux|en|The five ball '''angled''' off the nine ball but failed to reach the pocket.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[present]] or [[argue]] something in a particular way or from a particular [[viewpoint]].
#: {{ux|en|How do you want to '''angle''' this when we talk to the client?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|cue sports}} To hamper (oneself or one's opponent) by leaving the cue ball in the jaws of a pocket such that the surround of the pocket (the "angle") blocks the path from cue ball to object ball.

